# Patch files are kept byte-for-byte, with no line-ending conversion.
#
# Why this file exists at all. This repository is worked on from Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true, so git converts text files to CRLF on checkout. A .patch
# file is not prose: `git apply` compares its lines against the stored file
# content, which is LF. A patch checked out with CRLF can fail to apply against
# the very files it was generated from, with a "patch does not apply" that looks
# like a bad patch rather than a line-ending mismatch.
#
# -text switches the conversion off for these files only. Nothing else in the
# repository is affected.
*.patch -text
*.diff -text
